# terrain-claims.manifest - freecam poses for the retained-terrain claim census
# (tests/harness/check_terrain_claims.sh).
#
# One row per pose, the freecam corpus row form:
#   <level>[:<area>] | pos=(x, y, z) yaw=Y pitch=P | [start VBL] | [launch]
#   level   a --skip-to-level name; <level>:<area> enters the sub-area
#           (--skip-to-area)
#   pose    a freecam pose string (the per-tick freecam log format, verbatim)
#   start   the capture VBL (default: the freecam corpus's canonical VBL)
#   launch  tokens for this row's legs only (KEY=VALUE env entries, else
#           command-line arguments)
#
# Each row runs at --lod original and --lod extended with the retained cache
# forced on. Every row must read zero sectors claimed back to the CPU walk, in
# every claim class, on its last canonical walk at or before the capture VBL.
# The rows are freecam corpus poses, one or two per level, sub-areas included.
summer_forest | pos=(130413, 15471, 38359) yaw=1088 pitch=160
